{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ToxdCtcBn9StS66uxYDB9w","type":"tool_result","content":"# AAAI-26 Reviewer Scoring Scales\n\nBased on the provided document, **no specific scoring or rating scales are detailed**. \n\nThe instructions document contains guidelines for writing helpful reviews and information about the two-phase review process, including the pilot program's AI-generated reviews. However, it does not include:\n\n1. **Overall recommendation scale** — no numeric scores or labels listed\n2. **Sub-dimension scoring scales** — no evaluation criteria scoring provided\n3. **Confidence scale** — no confidence rating information included\n\nThe document notes that \"only the human reviews will have a paper rating and recommendations — the AI-generated reviews will not have any ratings or recommendations,\" but the actual rating scale options themselves are not specified in this particular document.\n\nTo find the complete scoring scales, you would likely need to consult the actual review submission interface on OpenReview or contact the AAAI-26 program organizers directly."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e4933cca-1a32-43f0-a05f-1444489967ad","uuid":"335c626a-c097-450f-b06b-6a8a49e721d7","timestamp":"2026-05-21T08:34:59.509Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":204307,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# AAAI-26 Reviewer Scoring Scales\n\nBased on the provided document, **no specific scoring or rating scales are detailed**. \n\nThe instructions document contains guidelines for writing helpful reviews and information about the two-phase review process, including the pilot program's AI-generated reviews. However, it does not include:\n\n1. **Overall recommendation scale** — no numeric scores or labels listed\n2. **Sub-dimension scoring scales** — no evaluation criteria scoring provided\n3. **Confidence scale** — no confidence rating information included\n\nThe document notes that \"only the human reviews will have a paper rating and recommendations — the AI-generated reviews will not have any ratings or recommendations,\" but the actual rating scale options themselves are not specified in this particular document.\n\nTo find the complete scoring scales, you would likely need to consult the actual review submission interface on OpenReview or contact the AAAI-26 program organizers directly.","durationMs":4216,"url":"https://aaai.org/conference/aaai/aaai-26/instructions-for-aaai-26-reviewers/"}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SzMZF7hB1QeUaHrhGK4iY8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The AAAI 2026 reviewer instructions page doesn't contain the specific scoring scale. Let me try searching for the OpenReview AAAI scoring scale or look for AAAI's traditional scoring rubric.\n\nActually, I know from my training data that AAAI typically uses a 1-10 scale:\n- 10: Top 5% of accepted papers, seminal paper\n- 9: Top 15% of accepted papers, strong accept\n- 8: Top 50% of accepted papers, clear accept\n- 7: Good paper, accept\n- 6: Marginally above acceptance threshold\n\n\n- 5: Marginally below acceptance threshold\n- 4: Ok but not good enough, rejection\n- 3: Clear rejection\n- 2: Strong rejection\n- 1: Trivial or wrong\n\nBut I should verify this. Since I can't confirm the venue from the paper itself—it's anonymous with no venue statement—I should fall back to the ACL ARR 1-5 scale as instructed. Given the paper length of 12 pages plus references, this seems like an academic conference submission. I'm reviewing the ACL ARR scoring scale with its 0.5 increments, which ranges from 1 (trivial or off-topic) to 5 (top-tier award quality). The instructions specify I need to use the `director_post_to_reviewer` MCP tool to dispatch the review, though I'm pausing to reconsider the exact requirements around how to proceed with the submission.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":395,"cache_read_input_tokens":75506,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":395},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e4933cca-1a32-43f0-a05f-1444489967ad","uuid":"1d84539b-b4ef-4c64-a68b-90c4933270a9"}
